            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to fight, then the Kannada for to retreat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ನಿಧನ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಿಧನ — nidhana — \"a passing away; a death\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಿರಿಯ ಲೇಖಕರ ನಿಧನದ ಸುದ್ದಿ ಬೆಳಗ್ಗೆ ಬಂತು. hiriya lēkhakara nidhanada suddi beḷagge bantu. The news of the senior writer's passing came in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The polite, formal word for a death, used in the news: ಅವರು ನಿಧನರಾದರು, he passed away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಿಧನ (nidhana) is borrowed from Sanskrit nidhana, \"settling down, residence\", and also \"conclusion, death\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
